{"id":"000VYD","title":"Annie's Song-doku","author":"MelancholicMoose","solvedCount":43,"difficulty":1,"rating":"96 %","firstSeen":"2026-11-08T15:19:29+00:00","posted":"Heute, 12:26 Uhr","rules":"Play online:\n\nSolve Annie's Song-doku on SudokuPad\n\nAnnie's Song-doku ❤\n\nMy very first published sudoku, created for someone\nwho makes my world brighter just by being in it.\n\nInspired by John Denver's \"Annie's Song\", this\nlittle puzzle is a celebration of love, nature, and\nthe beautiful way one person can fill another's\nsenses.\n\nHappy Birthday, my Annie. This one's for you.\n❤\n\nRules\n\nSudoku: Place the digits 1 to 9 exactly once\nin every row, column, and 3x3 box.\n\nRenban: Digits along each coloured line\nform a set of consecutive, non-repeating digits,\nin any order.\n\nKiller Cages: Digits in a dashed cage sum\nto the number in its top-left corner. Digits may\nnot repeat within a cage.\n\nXV: Cells separated by an X sum to 10.\nCells separated by a V sum to 5.\nNot all possible Xs and Vs are necessarily marked.\n\nThermometers: Digits strictly increase\nfrom the bulb towards the tip.\n\nQuadruples: Digits shown in a small circle\nmust appear at least once among the four cells\nsurrounding that circle.\n\nEven/Odd: Digits in cells marked with\na grey square must be even. Digits in cells\nmarked with a grey circle must be odd.\n\nPuzzle\n\nEnjoy the solve! ❤","solutionCode":"679258134814396527","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/js1ycm9h2n","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/js1ycm9h2n","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":9,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-08T15:19:29+00:00"}